    <string name="main_listener_on">On.</string>
    <string name="main_listener_off">Off. Allow "Aperture media and notifications".</string>
    <string name="main_aapm">Advanced Protection is on. Android blocks accessibility services that are not accessibility tools, so the island cannot draw until you turn Advanced Protection off. This is a system rule and no island app can work around it.</string>
    <string name="main_disclosure">What the accessibility permission is used for: drawing the island over the status bar, and knowing which app is in front so the island hides in camera apps. Aperture cannot read screen content, has no internet permission, and keeps nothing off your phone.</string>
